{
  "name": "Send website form leads to Google Sheets and Slack with an AI-drafted reply",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send website form leads to Google Sheets and Slack with an AI-drafted reply\n\n### Who's it for\nSmall sales teams and freelancers who get leads from a website form and want each one logged, shared and answered quickly.\n\n### How it works\n1. A **Webhook** receives the form submission (name, email, company, message, source).\n2. A **Code** node cleans the fields, validates the email and rejects bots that fill a hidden honeypot field.\n3. Invalid submissions get a `422` response listing the errors.\n4. For valid leads, an **OpenAI** chat model drafts a short first reply for a human to review. Nothing is sent automatically.\n5. The lead and the draft are appended to a **Google Sheets** tab that acts as a simple CRM.\n6. **Slack** posts the lead and the suggested reply to your sales channel, and the form gets a `200` response.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open the **Config** node and fill in your spreadsheet ID, sheet name, Slack channel, company name and reply tone.\n2. Create a sheet tab with this header row: `received_at, name, email, company, message, source, ai_reply_draft`.\n3. Connect your Google Sheets, Slack and OpenAI credentials on the matching nodes.\n4. Activate the workflow and point your form tool to the **production URL** of the webhook (POST, JSON or form-encoded).\n\n### Requirements\nn8n (Cloud or self-hosted), a Google account, a Slack workspace with a bot that can post in the channel, and an OpenAI API key (usage is billed by OpenAI).\n\n### Customization tips\nSwap OpenAI for Anthropic, Gemini or a local Ollama model, edit the prompt in **Draft reply with AI**, or replace Google Sheets with your CRM.\n\nQuestions? Ask in your order chat.",
        "height": 880,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "b75f98ec-9c1d-c9db-525c-3f58dd0ff644",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
